ing for the  disney plus platform he was very  insistent that these shows would not be  removed from the continuity of this  franchise's movies back in february 2019  feige told comicbook.com that these  disney plus programs would be quote  entirely interwoven within the  theatrical slate to phase 4 mcu releases  this was in sharp contrast how previous  tv shows based on marvel characters had  tended to function by and large they had  been mostly separate from the  feature-length narratives in the marvel  cinematic universe and phase four the  franchise has managed to live up to  feige's words one division set the stage  for wanda maximoff's villainous behavior  and doctor strange and the multiverse of  madness while ms marvel sets up its  titular superhero so that she can serve  as one of the leads of the 2023 project  the marvels  black widow's elena belova showed up in  a guest star capacity on hawkeye and  it's fair to assume that the falcon and  the winter soldier planted seeds that  would one day be sowed in thunderbolts  perhaps most importantly jonathan majors  debuted as a version of kang the  conqueror on loki before stepping into a  much larger role in movies such as  ant-man and the wasp quantomania and  avengers the kang dynasty it's clear  that feige's mission to narrow the gap  between big and small screen  storytelling has very much come to pass  looking back on the phase 4 movies  announced that the san diego  international comic con panel in 2019  you can immediately spot a few  recognizable titles projects such as dr  strange and the multiverse of madness  and thor love and thunder were among the  most exciting to be announced at the  event but one phase 4 film notable for  its absence was spider-man no way home  this was despite spider-man far from  home opening a few weeks before the  panel and going on to crack 1.1 billion  dollars worldwide it would later turn  out that its absence was no mistake  esony and marvel were in the middle of  negotiations at the time over the future  of spider-man this would eventually  result in the two companies parting ways  in august 2019 with sony planning to  continue the exploits of tom holland's  spider-man in their own movies  eventually an agreement was signed that  reunited the two companies to produce  another solar spider-man movie resulting  in spider-man no way home  in the first three phases of the marvel  cinematic universe it was difficult to  figure out how the franchise connected  to the broader franchise of netflix  characters such as daredevil jessica  jones luke cage and iron fist while  these shows would often reference mcu  events or characters the movies never  returned the gesture once the marvel  netflix shows were axed in late 2018 and  early 2019 it seemed like this chapter  of marvel storytelling had come to a  close but then came the absorption of  marvel television into marvel studios  the two entities had previously been  wholly separate complicating any  potential crossovers between their  projects however now that they were  under the same umbrella small screen  marvel projects could be more easily  ingrained into the wider mcu an  especially exciting example of this took  place in spider-man no way home in which  charlie cox's matt murdock makes a cameo  appearance it was the first time a  netflix character had appeared in an mcu  movie but it wouldn't be the last  vincent d'onofrio appeared as kingpin in  hawkeye cox returned for she-hulk and in  2022 marvel announced daredevil born  again a disney plus series slated for  release in 2024  to bring to life some of its disney plus  programming the various branches of the  walt disney company have turned to  turning screenplays for unproduced  movies into longer limited series the  most high profile example of this so far  has been obi-wan kenobi which utilized  enough key plot points and characters  from a planned movie to give that  feature screenwriter a full credit on  the project hello t