 how it might impact their  contractual obligations to the studio  but that has changed with phase four  with ryan coogler being the most notable  example of a director who opted to sign  on for the long haul as part of his  overall contract with disney coogler was  on the hook to oversee a new disney plus  marvel show set in wakanda at the end of  2021 it was announced that chongqi  director destin daniel creeton would be  humming a sequel to that movie and it  soon became clear that he had also  signed a long-term contract with marvel  studios sure enough in 2022 it was  reported that he would be directing  avengers the kang dynasty and overseeing  a wonder man series for disney plus for  phase 4 and beyond it seems that marvel  studios wants to keep a tight hold of  its most talented artists  [Music]

