tures came roaring back to  movie theaters and many managed to do  solid box office numbers however with  covet 19 vaccines still making their way  across the general populace people felt  varying degrees of comfort with going to  the movies this and plenty of other  factors doubtlessly impacted the  worldwide box office returns for the  first three installments in phase four  this trioa project scored the lowest  worldwide box office halls for any  marvel cinematic universe project  outside of the incredible hulk the black  widow being only the second project in  the series to make under 400 million  dollars globally however there is some  context needed to better understand  these grosses for starters black widow  is given a simultaneous premium video on  demand debut on disney plus which  doubtlessly cut into its grosses even  more importantly none of these movies  were released in china every marvel  studios project released in this  territory from 2017 to 2019 exceeded 100  million dollars with all three of the  companies 2019 productions grossing over  150 million dollars in china alone a  standard theatrical box office hall in  china would have boosted all three  movies past the 500 million dollar  worldwide mark still all three found  some form of box office success and  particularly chongqi which was briefly  the biggest domestic movie of 2021  before spider-man no way home returned  the franchise to its former box office  glory i love you guys  thank you  for phase 4 the mcu marvel studios has  tried to forge even deeper bonds than  usual with some of its most important  talent this is in sharp contrast to the  previous eras in the company's history  save for a three-year contract in 2012  keeping joss whedon around to work on  assorted projects marvel studios hasn't  kept filmmakers under long-term  contractual obligations this has made it  extra easy for directors like scott  derrickson and john watts to lead  prospective gigs without having to  navigate how it might impact their  contractual obligations to the studio  but that has changed with phase four  with ryan coogler being the most notable  example of a director who opted to sign  on for the long haul as part of his  overall contract with disney coogler was  on the hook to oversee a new disney plus  marvel show set in wakanda at the end of  2021 it was announced that chongqi  director destin daniel creeton would be  humming a sequel to that movie and it  soon became clear that he had also  signed a long-term contract with marvel  studios sure enough in 2022 it was  reported that he would be directing  avengers the kang dynasty and overseeing  a wonder man series for disney plus for  phase 4 and beyond it seems that marvel  studios wants to keep a tight hold of  its most talented artists  [Music]
 

